{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_f64_2", "label": "Fault F64.2 \u2014 a chain row is indivisible and so is not under the prime directive", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_tbstep", "label": "tbstep.py \u2014 channel-level division of a chain row", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Divides the row at its natural seam (the channel): solves the reference once, caches E_ref with its iteration count and guard rung, writes the cache by atomic replace before each next channel, stops at a declared budget reporting PARTIAL, and emits the row only when every channel resolves. It calls the same sealed nlchain/nlguard/ground functions with the same arguments, so nlchain.py is neither edited nor sed-ed."}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_prime_directive", "label": "Prime directive \u00a72.20 \u2014 work must divide and write intermediate results", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "nlchain restart is one process per row holding fourteen channel solves in a unit that either completes or returns nothing. At Z<=40 each row fitted a budget and the atom was never tested; at Z=89 ten converged channels were discarded at the wall-clock limit. A defect of the harness, not the physics \u2014 but one that costs time repeatedly and silently, which is what \u00a72.20 exists to prevent. The repair is admissible only because it was can-failed: Z=57 and Z=58 reproduce the sealed instrument with NO differing fields bar sec and driver."}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_orphan_determinism", "label": "The Z=57 orphan determinism receipt", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_f64_2", "target": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_tbstep", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_prime_directive", "target": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_f64_2", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_f64_2", "target": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_orphan_determinism", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_f64_2", "target": "recovered_fault_f63_2_reported_unshipped_result_f63_2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_orphan_determinism", "target": "recovered_fault_f60_2_induct_void_determinism_receipt", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F64.2-INDIVISIBLE-ROW.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_fault_f64_2_indivisible_row_tbstep", "target": "recovered_fault_f59_3_can_fail_the_fix", "relation": "references", "confidenc